{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Nintendo guided consolidated profit attributable to owners of parent to 200,000 million yen for the year ending March 31, 2021, down 22.7% year on year (PDF p. 2).",
      "citations": [
        {"passage_id": "P4", "quote": "Year ending Mar. 2021 | 1,200,000 | (8.3) | 300,000 | (14.9) | 290,000 | 200,000(19.5)(22.7) | 1,678.93"}
      ],
      "calculation_ids": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Against reported profit of 258.6 billion yen for the year ended March 31, 2020 (PDF p. 3), the 200.0 billion yen guide (PDF p. 4) implies a change of 200.0 − 258.6 = −58.6 billion yen, or (200.0 − 258.6) ÷ 258.6 × 100 ≈ −22.7%.",
      "citations": [
        {"passage_id": "P5", "quote": "net profit attributable to owners of parent totaled 258.6\nbillion yen for this fiscal year."},
        {"passage_id": "P2", "quote": "profit attributable to owners of parent of 200.0 billion yen."}
      ],
      "calculation_ids": ["C1", "C2"]
    }
  ],
  "analysis": {
    "text": "Base case at the results date: within ±2% of guidance, inclusive, for the year ending March 31, 2021. The main driver is shipment timing: production and shipping delays were easing (PDF p. 3), consistent with management’s assumption that Nintendo could meet full-year demand (PDF p. 4). If delayed consoles ship before year-end, the disruption shifts sales between quarters rather than costing Nintendo a full year’s worth of profit on those units.",
    "citations": [
      {"passage_id": "P1", "quote": "It appears that delays in production and shipping are gradually recovering."},
      {"passage_id": "P3", "quote": "we anticipate that production and sales will be able to meet demand for the full year"}
    ],
    "calculation_ids": []
  },
  "alternative_and_signal": {
    "text": "Downside alternative: persistent component shortages could leave Switch units unbuilt and orders unfilled by March 31, reducing full-year hardware sales and profit. I would switch to lower if Nintendo cut its full-year hardware shipment forecast because it could not secure enough parts. That would indicate lost fiscal-year volume, not merely a quarterly delay (PDF pp. 3–4).",
    "citations": [
      {"passage_id": "P1", "quote": "we may be affected if there continue to be\nissues involving the procurement of necessary components."},
      {"passage_id": "P3", "quote": "we anticipate that production and sales will be able to meet demand for the full year"}
    ],
    "calculation_ids": []
  },
  "direction": "within"
}

